1	//! Tool-call round-trip contract test for the OpenAI `/v1/chat/completions`
2	//! path, driven entirely on CPU through `pegainfer-sim`.
3	//!
4	//! This is the "protocol layer testable on pegainfer-sim" deliverable from the
5	//! coding-agent workstream (roadmap-2026-h2 §5). It does NOT test the upstream
6	//! vLLM tool parser in isolation (upstream already has `roundtrip.rs` for that).
7	//! It tests the seam pegainfer owns: a scripted engine byte stream ->
8	//! pegainfer's `TokenEvent` contract + detokenize -> upstream `Auto` parser
9	//! selection -> OpenAI `tool_calls` output, in both non-streaming and streaming
10	//! form.
11	//!
12	//! Several non-obvious constraints make this work — including two real wiring
13	//! gaps this test caught by failing (the frontend runs a *second* `Auto` parser
14	//! for reasoning; the upstream frontend suppresses the final token id on `Stop`,
15	//! so the script must pad a trailing EOS the engine never actually emits — see
16	//! #584). Each is documented at the code site it justifies rather than in a list
17	//! here, so the rationale stays next to the line it explains and can't drift.
18	
19	use std::fs;
20	use std::net::TcpListener;
21	use std::time::Duration;
22	
23	use anyhow::Context;
24	use anyhow::Result;
